l look at: intersexuality and supernumerary\u00a0genders; physical and cultural reproduction; sexuality; and sex-based and\u00a0gender-based violence and\u00a0power. We will use lectures, films, discussion sections and short field-based exercises.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(GLC-AS, SBA-AS, SCD-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(EC-LASP)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2825, "crseId": 357914, "crseOfferNbr": 4, "subject": "LGBT", "catalogNbr": "3250", "titleShort": "Staging Gay & Trans Histories", "titleLong": "Staging Gay and Transgender Histories", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 18297, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:20AM", "timeEnd": "01:50PM", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/05/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "slw42", "firstName": "Sara", "middleName": "L.", "lastName": "Warner"}], "pattern": "M", "facilityDescr": "Schwartz Ctr-Perform Arts 124", "bldgDescr": "Schwartz Ctr-Performing Arts", "facilityDescrshort": "SWZ124", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/17/2022", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "FGSS", "catalogNbr": "3250", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "FGSS", "catalogNbr": "6755", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "LGBT", "catalogNbr": "6755", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "PMA", "catalogNbr": "3755", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "PMA", "catalogNbr": "6755", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "VISST", "catalogNbr": "3260", "type": "B"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/22/2022", "sessionEndDt": "12/17/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "How have movements for sexual liberation used performance as a means of self-expression and\u00a0strategies for social justice? How have theatrical stages served as\u00a0sites of queer sociality and\u00a0crucibles of invention, where history is made and remade by social actors?", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(ALC-AS, LA-AS, SCD-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2825, "crseId": 359467, "crseOfferNbr": 3, "subject": "LGBT", "catalogNbr": "3740", "titleShort": "Parody", "titleLong": "Parody", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 16689, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:00PM", "timeEnd": "02:15PM", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/05/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "ngs9", "firstName": "Nick", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Salvato"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "To Be Assigned", "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": "TBA", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Class will meet in room 220 of the Schwartz Center."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/17/2022", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "AMST", "catalogNbr": "3745", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "FGSS", "catalogNbr": "3740", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "PMA", "catalogNbr": "3740", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/22/2022", "sessionEndDt": "12/17/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "In A Theory of Parody, Linda Hutcheon defines parody broadly as \"repetition with critical difference, which marks difference rather than similarity.\" Taking a cue from Hutcheon, we will consider parody as a form of meaning making that is not necessarily used in the service of ridicule. Rather, we will examine a number of late-twentieth- and early-twenty-first-century imitative works in order to distinguish the rich variety of political agendas and aesthetic rationales for recent parody. An emphasis on postmodern or contemporary performances and media that renovate images, ideas, and icons from modernism and modernity will unite our otherwise diverse efforts. Some of these efforts will also highlight what happens when an artist takes up a work made for one platform (for example, theatre, performance art, installation, cinema, television, the Web) and parodies it in another. Creators and works under consideration may range from Christopher Durang, Split Britches, and Pig Iron Theatre Company to The Simpsons, Cookie's Fortune, and Strindberg and Helium.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(ALC-AS, LA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2825, "crseId": 370485, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "LGBT", "catalogNbr": "3990", "titleShort": "Undergrad Independent Study", "titleLong": "Undergraduate Independent Study", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "IND", "ssrComponentLong": "Independent Study", "section": "601", "classNbr": 19167, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/05/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "slw42", "firstName": "Sara", "middleName": "L.", "lastName": "Warner"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/17/2022", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "IS", "instrModeDescrshort": "Indp Stds", "instrModeDescr"